# Core determinism

- No SFML / window / native graphics references in Core.
- No wall-clock time (`DateTime`, `Stopwatch`, `Environment.TickCount`) in simulation updates.
- No unseeded randomness. Seeds belong to the simulation.
- Gameplay-affecting iteration must be order-stable (prefer entity id ordering).
- Authoritative floating-point use is a multiplayer risk — isolate and document it.
- New mechanics need public testable APIs and Core unit tests without opening a window.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD
var roll = Random.Shared.Next();

// ✅ GOOD
// use simulation-owned seeded RNG or deterministic tables
```
